bodyguard-of-bits (0.4.4-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=high

  * Cross-distro terrain hardening release. One critical bug + three
    minor presentation fixes surfaced by terrain testing on Debian 13,
    Kali Rolling, Mint test, Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.
  * Critical: bob/checks/updates.py reported "system up to date" on
    100% of vierge Debian-family VMs (Debian 13 with 59 packages
    pending, Kali Rolling with 868, Mint with 33, Ubuntu LTS with 23
    of which 21 were security updates) because (a) `apt-get -s upgrade`
    is conservative and back-holds anything pulling a new package
    (typical kernel), (b) stale apt cache silently returned 0 packages.
    Now uses `apt-get -s dist-upgrade`, detects stale cache (mtime >
    7 days), cross-checks via `apt list --upgradable`, and propagates
    `updates_unknown` to the "Surface d'attaque" section instead of
    the false "up to date".
  * Minor: AppArmor "0 profiles loaded" dedicated key (was confusing
    on Kali); SMART check skipped when all disks are virtual; DDNS
    ports inlined in the WARN message.
  * Picked up the v0.4.3 audit-deferred items (S4 home-bounded
    symlink, M4 _parse_ufw_covered_ports refactor, I2 wave-2 key= on
    services and virtualization, locale-coverage test).
  * 4489 tests (+21 vs v0.4.3).

